# Milestone 9 — Voice Input (Speech-to-Text) Execution Log (TDD)

## Date: 2026-08-19
## Branch: `feature/m9-voice-input`

## Overview
Implemented voice-to-text input for the mobile app wizard using the
`speech_to_text` Flutter plugin, following a strict Red → Green → Verify TDD
cycle driven by the Gherkin contract in
`mobile_app/test/features/m9_voice_input.feature`.

---

## PHASE 1 — RED (Test-First)

### Files created (test-first)
- `mobile_app/test/voice_input_test.dart` — 6 widget test groups, one per
  Gherkin scenario:
  1. Requesting microphone permission on first use.
  2. Tapping the mic starts listening and updates the UI (pulsing glow,
     "Listening..." label, read-only field, permission caching).
  3. Converting speech to text and populating the input field.
  4. Handling microphone permission denial.
  5. Handling unrecognized speech.
  6. Handling speech recognition errors.

### Confirmed failure
`flutter test test/voice_input_test.dart` -> FAILED (compile error), expected:
```
Error when reading 'lib/core/mocks/mock_voice_input_service.dart': file not found
Error when reading 'lib/core/services/voice_input_service.dart': file not found
Error when reading 'lib/ui/molecules/wizard_voice_input_field.dart': file not found
'VoiceInputService' isn't a type.
Method not found: 'WizardVoiceInputField'.
Method not found: 'MockVoiceInputService'.
```
The tests could not even compile because the production abstractions did not
exist yet — the canonical RED state of TDD.

---

## PHASE 2 — GREEN (Implementation)

### Files created (implementation)
| File | Purpose |
|------|---------|
| `lib/core/services/voice_input_service.dart` | Abstract `VoiceInputService` contract: `initialize()`, `startListening(onPartial:)`, `stopListening()`, `isListening`, `status` stream, plus `VoiceInputStatus` enum (`idle, listening, done, notListening, unavailable`). |
| `lib/core/services/speech_to_text_voice_input_service.dart` | Real adapter wrapping the `speech_to_text` 7.4.0 plugin. The ONLY class importing the plugin. Maps plugin status strings (`listening`/`done`/`notListening`) to `VoiceInputStatus`, uses `ListenMode.dictation` + `partialResults: true`. |
| `lib/core/mocks/mock_voice_input_service.dart` | Test double implementing `VoiceInputService` (configurable `denyPermission`, `transcript`, `unrecognized`, `throwOnListen`; counts `initializeCalls` to verify permission caching). Mirrors `MockDietRepository`/`MockRoutineRepository` convention. |
| `lib/ui/molecules/wizard_voice_input_field.dart` | `WizardVoiceInputField` stateful widget: mic `IconButton` (idle `Icons.mic_none` / listening `Icons.mic`), pulsing `ScaleTransition` glow via `AnimationController`, "Listening..." label, read-only field while listening, inline error text for the three error cases. |

### Files modified
| File | Change |
|------|--------|
| `mobile_app/pubspec.yaml` | Added `speech_to_text: ^7.4.0` dependency. |
| `mobile_app/pubspec.lock` | Lockfile updated (added `speech_to_text`, `speech_to_text_platform_interface`, `speech_to_text_windows`, `json_annotation`; SDK upgrade bumped test-infra deps). |
| `mobile_app/android/app/src/main/AndroidManifest.xml` | Added `android.permission.RECORD_AUDIO` and `android.permission.INTERNET` (required for mic + network recognizer). |
| `mobile_app/ios/Runner/Info.plist` | Added `NSMicrophoneUsageDescription` (mandatory; iOS terminates on first mic access if missing). |

### Design decisions
- **Abstraction over plugin:** the wizard only depends on `VoiceInputService`;
  the real `speech_to_text` platform channel is never touched in widget tests
  (injected `MockVoiceInputService` instead). Same constructor-DI pattern as
  `HomePage`/repositories.
- **Permission caching:** `initialize()` is only invoked once; a second tap
  reuses the granted state (verified by `initializeCalls == 1` in Scenario 2).
- **Error model:** three distinct user-facing messages map to the three error
  Gherkin scenarios (permission denied, unrecognized, recognition failed).
- **Unrecognized/error cases keep previous value:** the field text is only
  replaced by a non-empty transcript; errors clear the transient error text
  but never wipe existing input.

